 \subsection{Unresolved Questions and Research Gap}
 
 The evidence reviewed also contains significant negative and, indeed, conflicting findings.
@@ -1097,27 +1105,4 @@ and treat them as equivalent evidence of generalisation.
 
 The 94 appraised works support a conditional benefit from multimodal monitoring. In four-state welding classification, combining image and audio raised accuracy from 90.2\% for the stronger single input to 96.1\%. In weld-penetration classification, both individual inputs and their combination reached 100\% on the clean test set \parencite{P003,Hua2026Weld}. In human--robot handover, adding gripper state to video and force/torque reduced five-class accuracy \parencite{Thoduka2024Handover}. Taken together, these comparisons locate the architectural question more precisely: for a given target and observation window, when does a second input retain complementary information, and when does a learned fusion rule use it more effectively than a strong single predictor or a fixed combination under the same fitting and reliability conditions?
 
